{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>I.</b> And how do You command me regarding my children, when the whole world is mine? For I made the earth and created man upon it. I, my hand spread out the heavens, and all their host I commanded and they were created. The sense is a parable of speech. And so it is written: \"For He commanded and they were created\" (Psalms 148:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {0 "The comment shifts between first and third person; rendered literally as the Hebrew demands, preserving Ibn Ezra's midrashic-style reading of the verse as though the prophet questions being commanded by God."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:11.001746559Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}